    "source": "",
    "copyright": "WHO Classification of Tumours Editorial Board. Head and neck tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; forthcoming. (WHO classification of tumours series, 5th ed.; vol. 9). https://publications.iarc.fr.",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 769px; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Affected sites</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Nomenclature (related/obsolete terminology)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4+ cell count</span></strong><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid black; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Salient clinical features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Pancreas</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related pancreatitis (autoimmune pancreatitis type&nbsp;1; lymphoplasmacytic pancreatitis)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup> (biopsy)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Parenchymal mass lesion mimicking pancreatic carcinoma (painless obstructive jaundice, pancreatic mass, abdominal pain) and/or pancreatic insufficiency (new-onset diabetes mellitus, steatorrhoea)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Sausage-shaped pancreas with delayed enhancement, capsule-like low-density rim, main pancreatic duct narrowing without upstream dilatation on contrast CT/MRI <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{32297064}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Hepatobiliary system</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related sclerosing cholangitis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup> (biopsy)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Biliary obstruction mimicking cholangiocarcinoma (obstructive jaundice, abnormal liver function tests) or primary sclerosing cholangitis but exhibiting dramatic response to steroids; frequently associated with IgG4-related pancreatitis</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Diffuse or segmental narrowing of bile ducts and wall thickening on cholangiogram <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{30575336}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related cholecystitis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup> (biopsy)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Mass lesion mimicking cancer (right upper quadrant pain, jaundice) <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{24944152}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related hepatic inflammatory pseudotumour</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup> (biopsy)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Probably represents intrahepatic involvement of IgG4-related sclerosing cholangitis</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Hepatic mass and abnormal liver function tests; contrast-enhancing mass lesion with dilatation of intrahepatic and peripheral bile ducts <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{31358425}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Orbit, including lacrimal glands</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related ophthalmic disease, IgG4-related orbital inflammation, IgG4-related orbital myositis (orbital pseudotumour, idiopathic fibroinflammatory disease, idiopathic orbital inflammation)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;400/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Unilateral or bilateral painless orbital swelling, proptosis and diplopia; rarely eye pain and visual impairment</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Contrast-enhancing soft tissue mass; preferentially affecting lateral rectus muscle in contrast to Graves ophthalmopathy; bilateral infraorbital nerve involvement on imaging is pathognomonic of IgG4-related ophthalmic disease <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{33068267;33402162;17414116}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Salivary glands</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related sialadenitis (K&uuml;ttner tumour, chronic sclerosing sialadenitis)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;400/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Unilateral or bilateral painless swelling most commonly involving submandibular gland; occasionally simultaneous bilateral lacrimal, parotid, and submandibular gland involvement (Mikulicz disease); xerostomia is usually mild and responds well to steroids in contrast to Sj&ouml;gren syndrome; sialography normal <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{26194097}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"3\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Retroperitoneum, mediastinum, and aorta</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related retroperitoneal fibrosis (Ormond disease)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;120/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Asymptomatic or nonspecific constitutional symptoms (fatigue, anorexia, fever, weight loss), low back or flank pain, leg oedema, abnormal renal function test</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Imaging shows soft tissue mass over paravertebral area and pelvis, frequently involving abdominal aorta and iliac arteries (IgG4-related periaortitis), and entrapping the ureter causing hydronephrosis <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{31942203;30754935}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related mediastinal fibrosis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;120/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Thoracic counterpart of retroperitoneal fibrosis and often manifest simultaneously; frequently involves thoracic aorta (IgG4-related aortitis/periaortitis); asymptomatic or dyspnoea, haemoptysis, dysphagia, and chest pain <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{29851832}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related aortitis&nbsp;/ periaortitis&nbsp;/ periarteritis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Most commonly involves infrarenal abdominal aorta and iliac arteries in the context of retroperitoneal fibrosis or thoracic aorta, less commonly other medium-sized arteries (coronary and mesenteric arteries); asymptomatic or low back pain; some may present with aortic aneurysm or dissection</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Imaging shows vessel wall thickening (media and adventitia), mass-like lesion with contrast enhancement with or without luminal dilatation (aneurysm) or reduction; PET-CT useful to assess disease activity and detect asymptomatic lesions <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{33121641;31942203}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Lymph node</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related lymphadenopathy</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;400/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Incidental lymphadenopathy on imaging, painless non-tender lymph nodes, often adjacent to organs affected by IgG4-RD, local mass effects (hydronephrosis, lower limb swelling for pelvic lymph nodes)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Lymph nodes usually mildly enlarged (mean: 20&nbsp;mm) with homogeneous enhancement and no calcification or necrosis <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{18344866;30558692}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Kidney</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related kidney disease</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup> (biopsy)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;120/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Incidental finding on imaging or abnormal renal function tests/urinalysis, hypocomplementaemia or elevated serum IgE is common</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Contrast CT shows multiple low-density lesions, diffuse kidney enlargement, and hypovascular solitary masses <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{33398598}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Dura and pituitary</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related pachymeningitis (idiopathic hypertrophic pachymeningitis)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;40/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Headache, cranial nerve palsies, visual impairment, motor weakness, numbness, seizures, cognitive decline, and gait instability <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{29061247;24384648}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related hypophysitis (lymphocytic hypophysitis)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"PT\">Headache, visual field defect, hyperprolactinaemia (galactorrhoea), hypopituitarism (diabetes insipidus, fatigue, amenorrhoea) <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{31929792;21593109}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Skin and soft tissue</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related skin disease (cutaneous pseudolymphoma)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related soft tissue disease</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">(Idiopathic cervical fibrosis; cutaneous pseudolymphoma)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;800/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Plaques or indurated nodules frequently in the head and neck region; local neurological symptoms (numbness and shoulder drop) due to associated nerve involvement are common <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{20871392}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Lung and pleura</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related lung disease, IgG4-related pleuritis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;80/mm<sup>2</sup> (biopsy)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;200/mm<sup>2</sup> (excision)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Incidental finding of abnormal chest imaging or cough, chest pain, dyspnoea, and haemoptysis</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Nodules, ground glass opacities, bronchial wall&nbsp;/ bronchovascular bundle thickening, interlobular septal wall thickening, infiltrative shadow, pleural thickening or effusion <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{26879484;31227290}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 121.906px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Thyroid</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.172px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"22%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-related thyroiditis (Reidel thyroiditis; fibrosing Hashimoto thyroiditis)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.0312px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&gt;&nbsp;80/mm<sup>2</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 365.391px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid black; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"53%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">At least some Reidel thyroiditis and the fibrosing variant of Hashimoto thyroiditis represent IgG4-RD; presents with goitre and/or hypothyroidism <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{33311000}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"ParaText\" style=\"margin: 6pt 0cm 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">IgG4-RD cannot be diagnosed solely on the basis of IgG4-positive plasma cell count.</span></p>",
